# The coiled styles' material: afro, coils, lowcut and wisps.
#
# A THIRD SHEET, and the split is measured rather than tidy-minded. The three
# hair materials differ only in how many strands their texture carries, because
# that number has to match what the geometry can resolve:
#
#   hair.mhmat       52 strands -- a SHELL or cap, many samples across `u`
#   hair_tube.mhmat   7 strands -- a swept TUBE, six or seven facets around
#   hair_card.mhmat   4 strands -- a CARD, exactly two columns in `u`
#
# A coil card spans u 0..1 with two vertices and draws a few pixels wide.
# Pointing the 52-strand sheet at it squeezed fifty-two strands across that
# span: rendered at head framing the hair showed a grid/moire pattern and the
# wisps style read as strips of tape. It had looked fine for as long as every
# render was full-body, where a card is sub-pixel and nothing about it is
# visible -- which is the argument for being able to render a close-up at all.
name Hair
tag MakeHuman™
ambientColor 0.04 0.03 0.02
diffuseColor 0.28 0.19 0.13
specularColor 0.6 0.6 0.6
shininess 0.3
opacity 1.0
transparent True
diffuseTexture ../hair_card_strands.png
backfaceCull False
castShadows True
receiveShadows True
shader data/shaders/glsl/litsphere
